From: SF2000 Linux Port <sf2000-linux@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] MIPS: sf2000: keep panel dark until controlled frame

The loader provides one health blink and then disables the backlight. Retained
RAM and UART already record all early progress, so the nonblocking kernel
helpers must not expose inherited ST7789 RAM or interfere with the atomic panel
reset and first-frame transaction.

Keep both progress helpers dark. The userspace display owner enables the
backlight immediately after it has written a complete controlled frame.

--- a/arch/mips/kernel/setup.c
+++ b/arch/mips/kernel/setup.c
@@ -649 +649 @@ void sf2000_visible_stage(const char *name, unsigned int pulses)
-	sf2000_backlight_set(1);
+	sf2000_backlight_set(0);
@@ -664 +664 @@ void sf2000_visible_tick(const char *name)
-	sf2000_backlight_set(1);
+	sf2000_backlight_set(0);
